     1	/**
     2	 * Laptop-independent nightly scanner for Nxeon.
     3	 *
     4	 * Runs on the Proxmox host via a systemd timer (see deploy/nxeon-nightly-scan.*),
     5	 * gathers real read-only signals about the running system, and writes deduped
     6	 * proposals into the `Improvement` table so the admin Improvements board
     7	 * (app/admin/improvements) keeps filling up even when the owner's laptop is off.
     8	 *
     9	 * Every signal collector is wrapped in try/catch so a single failure (e.g. no
    10	 * journal access) never aborts the whole run. Dedup: any proposal whose title
    11	 * already exists in an active improvement (PROPOSED | APPROVED | IN_PROGRESS) is
    12	 * skipped, so we never repropose the same finding night after night.
    13	 *
    14	 * The runner is CJS, so there is NO top-level await — everything runs inside
    15	 * main(), mirroring scripts/write-improvement.ts.
    16	 */
